# 🌍 Air Quality Monitoring System Using IoT

## ⚙️ Components Used

| Sr. No | Component | Description |
|--------|------------|-------------|
| 1 | Arduino UNO | Main microcontroller to process sensor data |
| 2 | MQ Sensors (MQ2, MQ3, MQ7, MQ135, MQ9, MQ4) | Detect gases like CO, CH₄, NH₃, Smoke, etc. |
| 3 | Single Channel Relay Module | Controls the exhaust fan based on gas level |
| 4 | Exhaust Fan (Brushless Motor) | Expels polluted air when harmful gases detected |
| 5 | 16x2 LCD Display | Displays real-time gas readings |
| 6 | GSM Module (SIM900A) | Sends alert message or calls when gas leakage occurs |
| 7 | Jumper Wires & Breadboard | For circuit connections |
| 8 | Power Supply | 5V – 2A input |

---

## 🔧 Working Principle

1. **Gas Detection:**  
   MQ sensors detect gases and send analog signals to Arduino.  
   The resistance of the sensor changes depending on gas concentration.

2. **Signal Processing:**  
   Arduino converts analog signals into readable values.

3. **Display:**  
   Real-time data is shown on a 16x2 LCD screen.

4. **Alert System:**  
   If gas level crosses a safe threshold, Arduino:
   - Activates the **Relay**, turning **ON** the exhaust fan.  
   - Sends an **SMS/Call alert** through the GSM Module.

---

## 🧩 Types of MQ Sensors and Their Working

| Sensor | Detectable Gases | Working Mechanism |
|---------|------------------|-------------------|
| MQ-2 | Methane, Butane, LPG, Smoke | Resistance of SnO₂ changes in presence of gas |
| MQ-3 | Alcohol, Ethanol, Smoke | Sensitive to alcohol vapors, gives analog signal |
| MQ-7 | CO, Methane, LPG | Detects CO; output changes with gas concentration |
| MQ-135 | Ammonia, Sulphide, Benzene Vapor | Wide range detection with built-in heater |
| MQ-9 | CO, Methane, LPG | High sensitivity, optimized for CO detection |
| MQ-4 | Methane, Butane, LPG, Smoke | Detects CH₄ and LPG with good accuracy |

